; The runtime: elements, the instance tree, reconciliation, hooks, context and
; scheduling. In React's terms this is [react] together with the reconciler, and
; emphatically not the renderer — nothing here draws anything.
;
; (libraries) is empty, and that is the load-bearing part of this file. Nothing
; in this directory may know what a wall, a pixel or an SDL window is: the
; reconciler is driven through Host.HOST and nothing else. Three things follow
; from that, and all three are the reason for the split:
;
;   - it can be tested against a mock host of plain strings, with no window
;     open and no renderer linked, which is what makes the hard part of this
;     engine testable as text;
;   - camlcast's own suite is untouched by anything that happens here;
;   - a second backend — a top-down view, a headless simulator — costs one
;     module implementing HOST rather than a fork.
;
; Adding camlcast to this line would compile. It would also silently delete all
; three, so it is a rule and not a preference.

(library
 (name camlcast_loom)
 (public_name camlcast.loom))
